I also replaced the old print-and-sentinel behavior with explicit exceptions: invalid capacity now throws `IllegalArgumentException`, and empty/full queue operations throw `IllegalStateException`. That removes the hidden `-1` contract and makes failures explicit.

Verified with `javac CircularQueue.java` and `java CircularQueue`; the sample run still prints:
```text
10 30
20 30
20 40
```

